  {\natexlab{c}}.
\newblock States that Learmonth RIMS uses three parabolic dish antennas to
  monitor 8 discrete frequencies (245, 410, 610, 1415, 2695, 4995, 8800,
  15400~MHz): a 28~ft (8.5~m) dish for 245/410/610~MHz, an 8~ft (2.4~m) dish
  for 1415--8800~MHz, and a 3~ft (1~m) dish for 15400~MHz. Output is digitised
  at 1~Hz and transferred to the Sydney World Data Centre. No RF/IF
  filter-response detail is published. Accessed July 2026.

